# Locales Kidux ships in, one per line, in /etc/locale.gen syntax.
#
# Every one of these has to be generated on the machine. A child's language is
# chosen in the adult panel, long after the installer ran and picked one locale,
# so the language a child needs is usually not the one that exists yet.
#
# Adding a language to Kidux means adding a line here. Nothing else generates
# locales, and no code has to change.
en_US.UTF-8 UTF-8
es_ES.UTF-8 UTF-8
